{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Managing the Restaurant", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Angry Customer", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe emotions and feelings in present and past situations in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.  ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.  ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The First Conditional: Possibility, Warnings and Threats", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the First Conditional with if-clauses to exchange opinions about possible future outcomes.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will or will not do something. In that condition, something else may, may not, will or will not happen. The outcome is not in the present, but in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">If you focus more on our customers, they'll leave a larger tip.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You also use the First Conditional to suggest a warning or a threat.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">If you don't focus on our customers, we'll keep on getting bad reviews.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structure:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If + Present Simple \u2026 will + verb \u2026</spa", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you can get the customer to calm down a little, you will be able to deal with their emotional state.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you can't diffuse the customer's anger, they will not hear you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If the customer doesn't think that you are working in their best interest, they will see you as part of the problem.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Willingness, Refusal, Promises and Threats ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> or <span class=\"italic\"> won't</span> to express willingness, refusal, promise and threat in situations in the present or in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are different ways to use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> or <span class=\"italic\">won't</span>. In the following uses, we don't necessarily talk about a future action or an event that will take place at a point in time in the future. Instead, <span class=\"italic\">will</span> or <span class=\"italic\">won't</span> are used to express willingness, refusal, promise or threat related to an action which could be in the present or in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the following examples:<ul><li>Willingness:</li> <span class=\"italic\">Will you clean the restaurant kitchen with me, please?</span> <li>Refusal:</li> <span class=\"italic\">I will not tolerate this behavior in the kitchen any longer.</span><br/><span class=\"italic\">The computer won't start.</span><li>Promise:</li> <span class=\"italic\">I'll do everything I can to satisfy our customers.</span> <li>Threat:</li> <span class=\"italic\">If you refuse to help me, I'll have to take extreme measures.</span></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If I don't speak to the manager soon, I will never come back here again!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will not be spoken to like that!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will do everything in my power to help you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Would you like to speak to the manager now?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Will you be able to come in tomorrow?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "emotional state ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the condition relating to your feelings ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You will be able to deal with their emotional state. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when dealing with a customer.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "willingness ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the state of being prepared to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need to show your willingness to listen carefully to their complaints. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to interject ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to interrupt what someone else is saying with a sudden remark ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Listen carefully to their complaints without interjecting with your own opinions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "attuned to ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "able to \u200bunderstand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need to show that you are attuned to their emotional needs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to acknowledge", "type": "name"}, {"content": "recognized as noticed or heard ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They want to be acknowledged as an individual. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "interaction", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the activity of talking to other people ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: At the end of your interaction with the customer, smile and thank them for allowing you to assist.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Work with a classmate to create a role play between a salesperson and an angry customer. (You can be a salesperson at any store. Use your imagination!)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think of reasons why a customer might be angry.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think of what a salesperson might do to alleviate this situation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a dialogue and write it down or take notes so you don't forget what you want to say. Remember to make it sound as natural as possible.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice the dialogue with your classmate.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Act out the dialogue for your class. Use appropriate body language.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss which dialogue sounded the most natural or the most polite.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write down what I want to say.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use expressions to soften the situation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice the dialogue out aloud with my classmate.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use body language to help express myself in the role play.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give feedback on the dialogues and discuss how they sounded.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn11le05ob03re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn11le05ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "", "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn11le05ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "All businesses have to deal with upset or angry customers so it's important to know how to deal with this situation. The first step is to address the situation and listen to the customer.\nIf you can get the customer to calm down a little, you will be able to deal with their emotional state. After you do this, you can then use specific problem-solving strategies to address the issue. If you can't diffuse the customer's anger, they will not hear you - they will not be receptive to what you are saying. He or she may become even angrier and react with a threat, \u201cIf I don't speak to the manager soon, I will \u2026 \u201d If the customer is agitated, you need to show your willingness to listen carefully to their complaints without interjecting with your own opinions.", "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn11le05ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "If you don't reduce the customer's emotional level, they will not be open to your suggestions. You need to show that you are attuned to their emotional needs. If the customer doesn't think that you are working in their best interest, they will see you as a part of the problem, instead of part of the solution.", "time": "51000"}, {"image": "engenn11le05ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "Remember that customers want to be respected. They want to be acknowledged as an individual, and they want to feel important and valued. As you interact with the customer, you should provide customer-focused responses to show the customer that your intention is to do whatever you can to meet their needs.", "time": "71000"}, {"image": "engenn11le05ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 4, "text": "Imagine you are a restaurant manager and a server tells you her customer wants to complain. You should go to their table, greet them with a smile and open gestures and body language. Allow the customer to fully explain the problem and vent their anger: \u201cI will not be spoken to like that!\u201d Show that you are listening and can empathize by using statements like, \u201cI see,\u201d \u201cI will do everything in my power \u2026 \u201d or \u201cI can understand how you must feel.\u201d Try to connect with the customer and let them know that you are on their side. When the problem has been identified and resolved, take the opportunity to apologize for any mistreatment, inconvenience or frustration. At the end of your interaction with the customer, smile and thank them for allowing you to assist. Inquire if there is anything else you can do for them, \u201cWould you like to/Would you like me to\u2026 ?\u201d", "time": "91000"}], "coverimg": "engenn11le05ob03re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about work and dealing with customers. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express that a fairly certain condition will be fulfilled using <span class=\"strong\"> <span class=\"italic\">when </span> </span>or <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">if</span></span>.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express willingness and refusal, and make promises and threats.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Have you ever been a difficult customer? Why? What happened? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Do you think it is important to stay calm and listen when a customer is upset? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "How do we deal with a difficult customer? ", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " Vanessa talks about dealing with a difficult customer, and how to <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">soften</span> the situation.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}, {"content": [{"content": "To <span class=\"italic\">\"soften\"</span> means to become less unpleasant or severe.", "type": "text", "tip_id": 0}], "type": "tips"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "STI", "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}]}]}, {"id": 2, "template_override": 3, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " Dealing with customers is very important.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Activity 1", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Listen to the text again. Select the correct answer.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You have 2 attempts to submit your answers. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob03re2aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": 3, "type": "template_override"}], "type": "DMC", "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "According to the narrator, the best way to deal with a customer with a problem is  ...", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "secondary_1", "type": "objective"}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "by interrupting them.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"correct": 0, "id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "by contradicting their ideas.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "id": 2, "text": "", "_data": [{"content": "by dealing with their emotions. ", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"correct": 0, "id": 3, "text": "", "_data": [{"content": "by taking them to a separate room.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}]}, {"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "You need to consider a person's emotional state, because otherwise ... ", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "secondary_1", "type": "objective"}], "id": 1, "responses": [{"correct": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "they will not listen to you. ", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"correct": 0, "id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "they will not come back. ", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"correct": 0, "id": 2, "text": "", "_data":